"Riseley, C. J.", "given_name": "C. J.", "family_name": "Riseley"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Roberts, I. D.", "given_name": "I. D.", "family_name": "Roberts"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Sethi, S.", "given_name": "S.", "family_name": "Sethi"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Shulevski, A.", "given_name": "A.", "family_name": "Shulevski"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Stein, M.", "given_name": "M.", "family_name": "Stein"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Stuardi, C.", "given_name": "C.", "family_name": "Stuardi"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Sweijen, F.", "given_name": "F.", "family_name": "Sweijen"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "ter Veen, S.", "given_name": "S.", "family_name": "ter Veen"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Timmerman, R.", "given_name": "R.", "family_name": "Timmerman"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Vaccari, M.", "given_name": "M.", "family_name": "Vaccari"}}, {"person_or_org": {"type": "personal", "name": "Wijnholds, S.", "given_name": "S.", "family_name": "Wijnholds"}}], "title": "The LOFAR Two-metre Sky Survey (LoTSS) VII. Third data release (HP-1078)", "publisher": "ASTRON", "publication_date": "2026-02-16", "subjects": [{"subject": "surveys"}, {"subject": "catalogues"}, {"subject": "radio continuum: general"}, {"subject": "techniques: image processing"}], "dates": [{"date": "2026-02-16", "type": {"id": "created", "title": {"cs": "Vytvo\u0159eno", "de": "Erstellt", "en": "Created", "sv": "Skapad"}}}, {"date": "2026-01-13", "type": {"id": "accepted", "title": {"cs": "P\u0159ijato", "de": "Angenommen", "en": "Accepted", "sv": "Accepterad"}}}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1051/0004-6361/202557749", "scheme": "doi", "relation_type": {"id": "isdescribedby", "title": {"cs": "Je pops\u00e1n (\u010d\u00edm)", "de": "Wird beschrieben von", "en": "Is described by", "sv": "Beskrivs av"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication", "title": {"cs": "Publikace", "de": "Publikation", "en": "Publication", "sv": "Publikation"}}}], "rights": [{"title": {"en": "Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC-BY-SA)"}, "link": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}], "description": "In this data release from the LOw-Frequency ARray (LOFAR) Two-metre Sky Survey (LoTSS) we present 120-168 MHz images covering 88% of the northern sky. The individual pointing images (at 6\u2032\u2032 and 20\u2032\u2032 resolution) were derived from 12,950 hrs (18.6 PB) of LOFAR High Band Antenna data which were processed through fully automated direction-independent and direction-dependent calibration pipelines that correct for instrumental effects as well as spatially and temporally varying ionospheric distortions. The Stokes I images were then combined, accounting for the rms noise level and telescope beam, to form the final Stokes I mosaic images at 6\u2032\u2032 and 20\u2032\u2032 resolution, with a central frequency of 144MHz. From the 6\u2032\u2032 resolution Stokes mosaics we derived a catalogue of 13,664,379 radio sources (consisting of 16,943,656 Gaussian components), the majority of which have never been detected at radio wavelengths before. These mosaics have a median rms sensitivity of 92 \u03bc Jy/beam; a random and systematic flux density scale accuracy of approximately 6% and 2%, respectively; an astrometric accuracy of 0.24\u2032\u2032; and we estimate that we detect more than 95% of sources with integrated flux densities exceeding nine times the local root mean square noise. This collection contains all the Stokes I mosaic products described above.<br><br>This is mosaic HP-1078.<br><br>Publication: Shimwell et al. 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202557749\">https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202557749</a>)<br><br>Go to <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.25606/SURF.lotss-dr3\">main LoTSS-DR3 Collection</a>"}, "custom_fields": {"c